<title>UK: Livshits expects one pct Russia growth in 1997.</title>
<headline>Livshits expects one pct Russia growth in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian economic growth should be around one percent next year, Finance Minister Alexander Livshits said on Friday.</p>
<p>Growth is expected to be about minus five percent this year.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope we will manage one percent of real growth of GNP (gross national product),&quot; in 1997, he told Reuters in London, where he is heading a roadshow to promote Russia's first international bond issue in more than 80 years.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Thatcher, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7770 (fax +44 171 583 7239)</p>
